Here is the corrected Turtle output:

```turtle
@prefix holon: <https://example.org/holon#> .
@prefix oe: <https://example.org/openevidence#> .
@prefix oeq: <https://example.org/openevidence/questions/> .
@prefix oegen: <https://example.org/openevidence/generated/> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<https://example.org/openevidence/questions/q_asthma_efficacy> a holon:ClinicalQuestionHolon .

<https://example.org/openevidence/questions/q_asthma_efficacy-int> a holon:InteriorGraph .
<https://example.org/openevidence/questions/q_asthma_efficacy-bou> a holon:BoundaryGraph .
<https://example.org/openevidence/questions/q_asthma_efficacy-pro> a holon:ProjectionGraph .
<https://example.org/openevidence/questions/q_asthma_efficacy-con> a holon:ContextGraph .

<https://example.org/openevidence/questions/q_asthma_efficacy>
  a holon:ClinicalQuestionHolon ;
  holon:hasInteriorGraph <https://example.org/openevidence/questions/q_asthma_efficacy-int> ;
  holon:hasBoundaryGraph <https://example.org/openevidence/questions/q_asthma_efficacy-bou> ;
  holon:hasProjectionGraph <https://example.org/openevidence/questions/q_asthma_efficacy-pro> ;
  holon:hasContextGraph <https://example.org/openevidence/questions/q_asthma_efficacy-con> ;
  oe:questionText "How effective is salbutamol compared with other agents for Asthma?" ;
  oe:answerText "Salbutamol is effective for Asthma." ;
  oe:hasAnswer <https://example.org/openevidence/drugs/salbutamol> .

<https://example.org/openevidence/drugs/salbutamol> oe:treats <https://example.org/openevidence/diseases/asthma> .
```

This output addresses the SHACL violations by:

1. Providing exactly one question text of >= 10 chars for the clinical question.
2. Including at least one answer for the clinical question.
3. Declaring exactly one interior graph, boundary graph, projection graph, and context graph for the holon.
4. Including the retrieved relation that answers the target question, which is the effectiveness of salbutamol for Asthma.
